 "meta": {"name": "Fujicolor Superia Venus 800", "maker": "Fujifilm", "kind": "colour-negative", "cine": false, "iso": 800, "balance": "daylight", "log_h_ref": null, "densitometry": "Status M equivalent", "process": "CN-16X", "grain": {"rms": 5}, "print_on": null, "document": "013AR284A", "date": "2003-01", "notes": ["Fujifilm product information bulletin (Japanese), page 4 plots; reference number 013AR284A, date read from the print code (営技・03.1-HB). Film sold as Superia Venus 800 (with a fourth, cyan-sensitive colour layer).", "Characteristic curves: daylight exposure 1/125 s, process CN-16X, Status M equivalent. x axis is log H in lux-seconds as printed; b/g/r are solid vector curves in blue/green/red, drawn from log H about -3.7 to 0.3 only.", "Spectral sensitivity: the sheet has no numbers on the y axis, only a scale arrow marking 1.0 (log unit) between two horizontal rules; y is therefore relative log sensitivity with 0 set at the lower rule and 1.0 at the upper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) needed for a specified density (minimum density + 1.0). Besides b/g/r the plot has the dashed cyan curve of the fourth colour layer (第4の感色層, cyan-sensitive layer), traced as line l4 (about 475-558 nm, peak near 515 nm, dashed); build.py ignores it. Each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.", "Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (中間濃度, density given by a neutral subject) and 'min' (最小濃度, minimum density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run 400-720 nm.", "Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 5 (printed as '……5' next to heading 10); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, sample density minimum density + 1.0. Film speed ISO 800/30 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 200 with LBB-12). No paper is recommended on the sheet."]}}